     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi folks - <br><br>I have an app I&#39;m working on, the gist of which (pun intended) is here:<br><br><a href=\"https://gist.github.com/jer-shiny/7270812\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://gist.github.com/jer-shiny/7270812&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792405049984000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3C-um3zbGb7MNci9LorX-f\">https://gist.github.com/jer-shiny/7270812</a><br><br>The behavior I want is, that the user uplaods a zip file of an ESRI GIS shapefile components, reads that into a dataframe, and then sends the field names of the read data frame to the selectInput.  Then, the user is able to see the renderPlot, which is dependent on the choice selected.  <br><br>However,<br><br>This app reads in the zip file, creates the dataframe, and nothing happens until I select the &#39;plot&#39; tab (ideally,  it&#39;d be nifty if I could update the selectInput box while still in the default &#39;instructions&#39; tab).  Then when I do choose the &#39;plot&#39; tab, the app immediately goes to try and build the plot - without first filling in the selectInput with the proper choices or enabling the user to select one.  <br><br>How do I go about obtaining the desired behavior?  <br><br>I accept any and all hints.  Thanks!<br><br><br><br><br></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
